      en: "The Baffin mining project, primarily the Mary River iron ore mine on Baffin Island, is one of Canada's most significant mining developments in the Arctic. Operated by Baffinland Iron Mines, it produces high-grade iron ore with a content exceeding 66% iron, essential for steelmaking. The ore is transported via a 100-kilometer railway to the port at Milne Inlet for shipping. The project has boosted Nunavut's economy, providing employment and infrastructure, but faces environmental challenges regarding wildlife and permafrost. Production capacity is targeted at 6 million tonnes per year.",
